Phase 2 (FullSpectrum engine emission, P2I): register the FS dithering
+ mixed-filament keys in PrintObject's `invalidate_state_by_config_options`
key lists so config changes force a re-slice.

Ported from FS v0.9.9 (`ratdoux/OrcaSlicer-FullSpectrum@v0.9.9` commit
b3c41fda), `src/libslic3r/PrintObject.cpp` +9 LoC across two existing
invalidation blocks.

Why this matters:

`PrintObject::invalidate_state_by_config_options` is consulted on every
incremental Print::apply diff — when a key in the lists changes,
specific PrintObject steps (slice / perimeters / etc.) are invalidated
and re-executed. Keys NOT in any of the lists silently get treated as
"no engine effect" and the prior slice state is reused.

Our v2.3.2 had none of the FS dithering / mixed-filament / region-
override keys in any invalidation list. End user symptom: change the
Local-Z mode toggle in the UI between slices and the second slice
silently reuses the first slice's region geometry; the user wonders
why the print didn't change.

Added two blocks:

1. The `posSlice` block (lines ~1083): adds
   `dithering_z_step_size`, `dithering_local_z_mode`,
   `dithering_local_z_whole_objects`,
   `dithering_local_z_direct_multicolor`,
   `dithering_step_painted_zones_only`,
   `mixed_filament_component_bias_enabled`,
   `mixed_filament_region_collapse`. These affect cadence + region
   geometry so they force a full slice.

2. The infill-filament block (lines ~1218): adds
   `enable_infill_filament_override`,
   `infill_filament_use_base_first_layers`,
   `infill_filament_use_base_last_layers`. These shift the effective
   infill filament for boundary layers so they force the infill +
   perimeter re-run.

Verified compile-clean via incremental libslic3r rebuild (3/3 objects,
0 FAILED) + ./gradlew :app:assembleDebug.

Hard dependencies:
  - patch 0027 (PrintRegionConfig + PrintConfig fields declared as
    typed members)

